  "description": "The stack premise. The parser descends once per nesting level and refuses an object or array opened past 512 levels by name, before it descends: a document nested 512 deep is read, one nested 513 deep or more is `refused` with `LimitExceeded/depth`, however deep it goes. Each vector gives `input`: the text is `open` repeated `depth` times, then `inner`, then `close` repeated `depth` times. An accepted document's answer is `accepted`, the SHA-256 (lower-case hex) of its canonical rendering, which is the text itself. A host reproduces every answer on the SMALLEST stack it supports, so the 512-deep documents are read without exhausting it and the deeper ones are refused rather than overflowing it.",
